{%- comment -%}
  IMAGE BRIEF PLACEHOLDER

  Renders where a real image should go, and tells whoever is filling the site
  exactly what to put there, subject, aspect, minimum pixels, max file size.
  It disappears the moment an image is uploaded to the block's image_picker.

  This is deliberately not a pretty grey box. A placeholder that doesn't say
  what it wants gets ignored; one that reads like a shot list gets filled.

  Params:
    label, slot name, e.g. "HiTork · hero"          (required)
    brief, one line on what the photo should show    (required)
    ratio, e.g. "24:9"                               (required)
    min_w, minimum width in px, e.g. 1600            (required)
    weight, max file size, defaults to "250 KB"
    tone, 'light' (default) or 'dark'
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign weight = weight | default: '250 KB'
  assign tone = tone | default: 'light'
-%}

<span class="img-brief{% if tone == 'dark' %} img-brief--dark{% endif %}" role="note">
  <span class="img-brief-inner">
    <span class="img-brief-tag">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-camera"/></svg>
      Image needed
    </span>
    <span class="img-brief-label">{{ label }}</span>
    <span class="img-brief-copy">{{ brief }}</span>
    <span class="img-brief-specs">
      <span><b>Ratio</b>{{ ratio }}</span>
      <span><b>Min width</b>{{ min_w }}px</span>
      <span><b>Max size</b>{{ weight }}</span>
      <span><b>Format</b>JPG / WebP</span>
    </span>
    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      <span class="img-brief-how">Upload in Customize → this section → Image</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
</span>
